    // detectors the emitter covers and by nothing else", which reads as an instruction to make
    // the fires bigger, and it was the standing next step for this row. It is not needed and it
    // would be paid for in the wrong currency \u2014 a fire is 1.2 m per detector at 12 deg and 3.6 km,
    // so 3x is a burning building 21 m across. Every figure that motivated it, including the two
    // above, was taken at 1352x1014; reduced to the 352x240 picture raster the reference lives at,
    // the emitters' own contribution to the flicker is ALREADY ZERO. See the volumeTau option
    // for the measurement and the positive control that proves the instrument still sees the
    // defect when it is put back.
